1a:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":"Source: WordStream 2026 Google Ads Benchmarks - 13,000+ search campaigns, April 2025 to March 2026. Unit: search-campaign conversion rate averages, not single-page rates."}]
1b:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Why the widely-cited 2.35% figure is the wrong benchmark"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The 2.35% figure circulates widely as “the average landing page conversion rate.” It originates from a 2012 Unbounce dataset reproduced in a 2014 blog post. Using a 12-year-old figure as a current benchmark for paid search performance is not informative - the traffic landscape, mobile adoption rates, and advertising platform sophistication have all changed substantially."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"More importantly, the 2.35% figure was an all-traffic median - mixing organic, direct, email, and paid together. Paid search conversion rates are structurally higher than that figure because paid search visitors arrive with explicit purchase intent. The correct comparison for a paid search landing page is the WordStream 2026 data above, not a 2012 all-traffic median."}]]}]
1c:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Traffic source is the largest variable"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Traffic source determines how warm and how intent-qualified the visitor is when they land. The same page with the same offer can show dramatically different rates by source."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4","children":[["$","li","Paid search (Google Ads)",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Paid search (Google Ads)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Highest intent of the paid channels. Visitor was actively searching for a solution. WordStream 2026 all-industries average: 8.18%. Use vertical-specific figures for comparison."}]]}],["$","li","Paid social (Meta, TikTok, LinkedIn)",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Paid social (Meta, TikTok, LinkedIn)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Interruption traffic - the visitor was not searching for your offer. Conversion rates are structurally lower. Comparing paid social rates against the WordStream paid search benchmark will always make your page look underperforming."}]]}],["$","li","Email (owned list)",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Email (owned list)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Warmest traffic type. Visitors already trust the sender. Email traffic to a landing page commonly converts at 2–5x the rate of cold paid traffic on the same page."}]]}],["$","li","Retargeting",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Retargeting"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Visitor has already seen your brand or page. Higher conversion rate than cold traffic from the same channel by design - this is the expected retargeting premium, not a page quality signal."}]]}]]}]]}]
1d:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"How to use benchmarks as a diagnostic tool, not a verdict"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A conversion rate below the vertical benchmark is a signal that something is broken - not a conclusion about which thing is broken or how bad it is. The right response to a low rate is to run a signal-level diagnosis:"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-3","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[1,"."]}],"Segment by source and device - confirm the low rate is present on the channel you are optimising for, not an artefact of a high-bounce source dragging the overall number down."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[2,"."]}],"Check load time - if LCP is above 4 seconds on mobile, fix that before anything else. You cannot diagnose copy or layout problems if visitors are bouncing before the page renders."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[3,"."]}],"Run the 9-signal check - message-match, trust, mobile layout, load time, CTA clarity, form friction, proof. The first broken signal is the first fix. Earlier signals gate later ones."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[4,"."]}],"Compare against the right benchmark - your vertical, your traffic source, your offer type. A B2B SaaS lead-gen page at 4% compared against an e-commerce transaction benchmark is a category error."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"You need at least 500 paid traffic sessions to a single page before your conversion rate is statistically meaningful. Below that, a single unusual week can shift a 3% rate to 8% and back without the page changing. Focus on structural signal checks before optimising toward a number."}]]}]
